<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    Ravenroot development harness — SOURCE ONLY. THIS MODULE IS NEVER PUBLISHED.

    It exists because the shipped distribution cannot register a ModelProvider and must not be able
    to: P3 of ravenroot-distribution's ReleaseArtifactBoundaryChecks makes a call to
    ModelProviderRegistry#register reachable from RavenrootServerMain#main a release violation,
    because the released artifact must not compose a model adapter into itself: the embedding seam
    is supplied from outside the artifact, or it is not supplied. Ravenroot's qualification as an
    upstream component under EU AI Act recital 89 rests on the shipped artifact not performing that
    composition, as captured by ADR 0017.

    THIS MODULE ALSO SUPPLIES THE NODE, not only the provider. llm-prompt is absent from the core
    catalogue and default image, so the bench carries its own
    ai.ravenroot.devharness.LlmPromptNodeBehaviorFactory and registers it on top of
    BehaviorRegistry.standard(...). Without that factory the provider registry would have no
    consumer and the bench would not exercise its advertised path.

    So the composition lives here instead, in a program with its own coordinates that is never built
    into anything anyone receives. Five conditions define this module, and THREE of them (1, 2
    and 4) are facts enforced by the build rather than sentences in a comment. The other two are not,
    for different reasons: condition 3 has no control that could observe it, and condition 5 is
    itself a line in a document, which is the very thing the phrase above contrasts with. An earlier
    revision of this header said "four", which quietly counted condition 5 as enforced:

      1. NEVER PUBLISHED. maven.deploy.skip and maven.install.skip below make `mvn deploy` and
         `mvn install` publish nothing, anywhere, including the local repository. There is no
         registry, no GitHub Packages entry, no GHCR image, no release asset.
      2. NEVER SERVED ON A REACHABLE NETWORK. DevHarnessMain forces the loopback address and ignores
         RAVENROOT_BIND_ADDRESS. Serving a network would be putting into service under art. 3(11),
         and "for testing" is not an exemption. DevHarnessMainTest pins it: every wildcard, LAN
         address and hostname form is replaced by loopback, and the authenticator is decided from
         that same forced value, so the socket and the auth decision cannot drift apart.
      3. NEVER USED FOR PRODUCTION WORK. NO CONTROL HERE CAN ENFORCE THIS ONE. It is an operational
         constraint, and it is stated as one.
      4. STRUCTURAL, NOT DECLARED. The name says what it is; README.md says it is not a release
         artifact; and NotAReleaseArtifactTest fails the build if these coordinates appear in any
         release, publish or deploy surface.
      5. EXCLUDED FROM RELEASE ARTIFACTS. The structural checks above enforce this directly.

    NEVER add this module to ravenroot/pom.xml's <modules>. NotAReleaseArtifactTest checks that too.

    Build order: the reactor and the adapter must be installed first, because this project resolves
    its Ravenroot dependencies from the local repository rather than from reactor siblings.

        ./dev.sh          <- performs the three steps below, selecting a JDK 21..25 itself

    The command above is the recommended approach. To run the sequence manually with JAVA_HOME in range:

        mvn -f ravenroot/pom.xml install -pl ravenroot-server,ravenroot-pekko -am -DskipTests
        mvn -f ravenroot-adapter-openai-compatible/pom.xml install
        mvn -f ravenroot-dev-harness/pom.xml verify

    Note the asymmetry, which is deliberate: the ADAPTER is installed (an operator has to be able to
    put it on a classpath), and this HARNESS is not (nobody may).
-->
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <groupId>ai.ravenroot.devharness</groupId>
    <artifactId>ravenroot-dev-harness</artifactId>
    <version>0.1.0-alpha.1</version>
    <name>Ravenroot Development Harness (never published)</name>
    <description>
        Source-only local bench that starts Ravenroot with an llm-prompt node it supplies itself and
        a model provider registered, so that node can be exercised from the editor on a developer
        machine. The core ships neither half. Not a release artifact. Never published,
        never network-facing, never used for real work.
    </description>

    <properties>
        <maven.compiler.release>21</maven.compiler.release>
        <project.build.sourceEncoding>UTF-8</project.build.sourceEncoding>
        <project.reporting.outputEncoding>UTF-8</project.reporting.outputEncoding>
        <ravenroot.version>0.1.0-alpha.1</ravenroot.version>
        <junit.version>6.1.2</junit.version>

        <!--
            Condition 1, as a fact about the build rather than a promise about behaviour. `mvn deploy`
            on this module publishes nothing to any repository, and `mvn install` does not even put it
            into the local one, so no other project on this machine can depend on it by accident,
            which is the realistic first step towards it being used for something. Removing either
            line is a visible edit in the file whose entire header says why they are here, and
            NotAReleaseArtifactTest fails if either goes missing.
        -->
        <maven.deploy.skip>true</maven.deploy.skip>
        <maven.install.skip>true</maven.install.skip>
    </properties>

    <dependencies>
        <!-- The HTTP adapter and its composition types. Brings ravenroot-core transitively. -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>ai.ravenroot</groupId>
            <artifactId>ravenroot-server</artifactId>
            <version>${ravenroot.version}</version>
        </dependency>
        <!-- The execution engine, chosen at runtime exactly as ravenroot-sample chooses it. -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>ai.ravenroot</groupId>
            <artifactId>ravenroot-pekko</artifactId>
            <version>${ravenroot.version}</version>
            <scope>runtime</scope>
        </dependency>
        <!--
            The thing being armed. This dependency, together with the llm-prompt factory this module
            now carries in src/main, is the reason it may not be published: an artifact combining the
            runtime with a generative node AND a registered ModelProvider is no longer an upstream
            component, it is a composed AI system.
        -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>ai.ravenroot.adapters</groupId>
            <artifactId>ravenroot-adapter-openai-compatible</artifactId>
            <version>${ravenroot.version}</version>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.junit.jupiter</groupId>
            <artifactId>junit-jupiter</artifactId>
            <version>${junit.version}</version>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
    </dependencies>

    <build>
        <plugins>
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-enforcer-plugin</artifactId>
                <version>3.6.1</version>
                <executions>
                    <execution>
                        <id>enforce-java-version</id>
                        <phase>validate</phase>
                        <goals><goal>enforce</goal></goals>
                        <configuration>
                            <rules>
                                <requireJavaVersion>
                                    <version>[21,26)</version>
                                    <message>Ravenroot builds on JDK 21 through 25; JDK 26 is not a supported build platform.</message>
                                </requireJavaVersion>
                            </rules>
                        </configuration>
                    </execution>
                </executions>
            </plugin>
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-compiler-plugin</artifactId>
                <version>3.15.0</version>
            </plugin>
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-surefire-plugin</artifactId>
                <version>3.5.6</version>
            </plugin>
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.codehaus.mojo</groupId>
                <artifactId>exec-maven-plugin</artifactId>
                <version>3.3.0</version>
                <configuration>
                    <mainClass>ai.ravenroot.devharness.DevHarnessMain</mainClass>
                </configuration>
            </plugin>
        </plugins>
    </build>
</project>
